  "id": "compound-action-potential",
  "term": "compound action potential",
  "definition": "A compound action potential is the electrical signal produced by a group of activated nerve fibers and recorded at a contact or electrode. In this context, an evoked compound action potential reflects the combined response of nerve fibers activated by spinal cord stimulation.",
